I've fixed the image build so this can't ship again and queued the fix to land on main, but my own full-gates build of it came back red. The published `build:*` images still carry the CVE until they are rebuilt.

**Cause:** upstream had already fixed it. `docker:29-cli` moved to Docker 29.10.0, built with go1.27.4, at 2026-11-16 22:07Z. Every published `build:*` image was built before that (`latest` on 11-15, each `X.Y` around 14:05Z on 11-16), so they all kept 29.9.3's go1.26.10 docker binary.

**Change (on `looper/tacplus-901`, queued with the manager):**
- **20b9bf9a:**
  - `images/smoke.sh` gets a new check, `go_stdlib_check`. The image's smoke test now refuses a docker CLI built with a Go older than the fixed release on its line (go1.26.11 for 1.26, go1.27.4 for 1.27). A rebuild that picks up an unfixed CLI fails instead of being published.
  - `scripts/images_smoke_test.go` adds `TestSmokeGoStdlibCheck`, written first and failing before the check existed.
  - `images/build.Dockerfile` gets a note explaining this. Because that file changed, the push to main also rebuilds `build:latest`.
- **3e42f085:** a PROPOSALS.md entry. Nothing rebuilds `build:*` when an upstream image it copies from moves, which is why the nightly sweep kept failing for days after the fix was published.

**Verification:**
- `go test ./scripts` passes locally, and the rest of `go test ./...` showed no failures in the packages that build without generated code.
- Against the real upstream binaries, the check refuses docker 29.9.3 and accepts 29.10.0.
- **The full-gates build of 20b9bf9 (pipeline 3092205090) was red:** `OVERALL fail=1`. I can't read the build project's logs (404), so I don't know which gate failed. #778 got the same `fail=1` on two unrelated changes on this main, so main itself is probably red. My diff changes no input to any gate except `go test ./scripts`. I landed anyway because the manager rebuilds the batch and bisects on red.

**Release and backports:** I tagged nothing on main. Main has taken features since v2.6.1, and v2.6.2 through v2.6.13 already exist. Backport PRs are open against each release line, and each names the patch tag to cut once it merges (or the next free one if another backport's tag is cut first): #910 (2.0, v2.0.33), #911 (2.1, v2.1.26), #912 (2.2, v2.2.23), #913 (2.3, v2.3.25), #914 (2.4, v2.4.25), #915 (2.5, v2.5.26), #916 (2.6, v2.6.14).

**Not done:** I tried to start the line rebuilds now, but the token isn't allowed to trigger workflows (403). The weekly schedule rebuilds every `build:X.Y` on Mon 2026-11-23 at 05:23Z.

**Left for the next run, after the manager's verdict:**
1. If the land comes back red, fix it and land again.
2. Once merged, confirm `build:latest` was rebuilt and that trivy shows no CVE-2026-97054 on `build:latest` and on `build:2.0`–`build:2.6` after 11-23.
3. Confirm the next Nightly security run passes "Published images".
4. Post the outcome comment (no handlers touched; the trace check's 8 existing findings are tracked in #311) and close the issue.
